Hardware CI: circuit extraction from real board files, device-model binding,
static checks, and firmware co-simulation on emulated MCUs.
https://hauksbee.dev

This product includes software developed by Eoghan Collins.

The Altium .PcbDoc binary record layouts used by the Altium ingest were
ported field-by-field from the record-layout descriptions in KiCad's Altium
importer (Copyright the KiCad Developers, GPL-3.0). See
docs/ingest/ALTIUM.md and docs/about/release-and-licensing.md for the
provenance and licensing position.

The RP2040 co-simulation platform embeds third-party files, which the binary
therefore redistributes:

  - Renode peripheral models for the RP2040 (C# sources), copied byte-for-byte
    from matgla/Renode_RP2040, Copyright Mateusz Stadnik, MIT.
  - RP2040.svd, from the Raspberry Pi pico-sdk, Copyright 2020 Raspberry Pi
    (Trading) Ltd., BSD-3-Clause.
  - The RP2040 boot ROM image (bootrom.elf), from
    raspberrypi/pico-bootrom-rp2040, Copyright 2020 Raspberry Pi (Trading)
    Ltd., BSD-3-Clause.

Full licence texts ship beside those files in
crates/hauksbee-mcu/db/mcu/rp2040/, whose README.md records the exact upstream
commits and tags.

